{"availability":"available","full":"vesvault/vespost","name":"vespost","description":"End-to-end encrypted collaborative sticky notes — a ~300-line libVES.subtle.js reference app with in-browser encryption, per-note sharing & roles, key recovery, and an authoritative change log. No app server.","category":"Productivity","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-05-02T02:54:57Z","updated":"2026-07-10T00:52:58Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://demo.ves.world","topics":["access-control","audit-log","client-side-encryption","collaboration","demo","e2ee","encrypted-notes","end-to-end-encryption","javascript","key-recovery","libves","reference-app","serverless","sticky-notes","vesvault","zero-knowledge"],"demo":"https://vesvault.github.io/vespost/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:39.638Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:39.638Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:39.638Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:09:39.638Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["VESpost is a 300-line, single-page web app that lets people keep shared notes that are encrypted in the browser before they ever leave the device, share each note with other people by email, and see an authoritative history of every change — who changed what, when — with no application server of your own to run.","It is a working reference for building collaborative, end-to-end encrypted apps on libVES.subtle.js. The \"sticky notes\" are just a thin UI over a much more general primitive: a shared, versioned, end-to-end encrypted record store with live sync, per-record access control, and an authoritative change log.","Most \"E2EE\" apps make you choose between security and usability. VES doesn't, and VESpost demonstrates four things that are normally hard, each of which you get essentially for free from libVES.subtle:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vesvault/vespost/b